<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orkneyinga saga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1200</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Orkneyinga saga is an Old Norse saga written in Iceland around 1200 that tells the history of the earls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> from the Norse settlement to the late 12th century. It includes the lives of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thorfinn-the-mighty">Thorfinn the Mighty</a>, the martyred Earl Magnus and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rognvald-kali-kolsson">Rögnvald Kali Kolsson</a>. It is the main written source for the Norse earldom of Orkney.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orkneyinga-saga.jpg" alt="Orkneyinga saga" width="320" height="535" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See 'source' above. The actual handwriting is that of Magnus Thorhallson. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flatey_Book,_Orkneyinga_saga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
